  // The number here is the release rule doubled, so the rule travels with it.
  // The line used to print the doubled figure alone, which left the learner
  // to reverse-engineer what clears a question from an unexplained total
  // (reported by the maintainer, 2026-09-16). Three things are needed to make
  // the figure add up and none of them was stated: a round covers the whole
  // list before anything repeats (finishStudyPass rebuilds the queue and
  // resets the index, so a question answered right once returns on the NEXT
  // round, not immediately), two correct in a row release a question, and a
  // miss restarts it, which is the only thing making "at least" honest.
  // The word is ROUND, not pass: "pass" means something else in an exam app.
  //
  // Since 2026-09-17 the release rule is level-aware (drillCleanRun), so the
  // figure is no longer the question count doubled and the line no longer
  // promises "at least two rounds": a list whose questions all owe a single
  // answer clears in one. The total is summed per question now, so it also
  // counts down as the learner answers instead of only when one is released.
