// tests can sit third: card 4567's hitch statement (24094) lands on a bullet
// that opens with the electrical connection, so the reader arrives at a line
// about something else and concludes the button is broken. Splitting every
// such bullet is not the answer, since many of them are one membership list
// that belongs together (778 statements land past the first sentence of their
// block). So the app highlights the sentence inside the block instead.
//
// The choice is made on the ITALIAN block, where the words match the
// statement, and the index is reused for the English, which is translated
