// The same estimate recomputed on a five-day week: the learner's own
// per-STUDY-day pace, spread over five days in seven. The main date above runs
// on the CALENDAR rate, which is whatever pattern of work and rest the last
// fortnight actually held, so the two answer different questions and both are
// shown (maintainer's decision, 2026-09-16).
//
// It was offered only to a learner with no rest days at all, on the reasoning
// that the observed pattern speaks for itself. It does, but it does not
// answer the question the Help raises, which is what a steady five-day week
// would cost; and the condition made the line vanish for exactly the learners
// resting three or four days a week, for whom the five-day figure is the more
// useful of the two. Where someone already rests two days in seven the two
