// Misses at this level, counted so that nothing can erase them.
// `seen - correct` was the only available measure until 2026-09-19 and remains
// the fallback for a record written before the counter existed, but it is NOT
// stable: liftCredit raises `correct` when a HIGHER level masters a statement
// and `seen` follows it up, which silently erases the evidence that a lower
// level ever missed it. Measured on a real export that day: sixteen statements
// reading clean at L1 and L2 carried the signature of an erased miss, against a
// 3% background rate, which was enough to bias "did I know this when the
// English was there?" in the flattering direction. The counter is written on
// the wrong answer itself, preserved before any lift, and max-merged by sync.
