// lesson: it described the conditional cancel that a later pass removed, so it
// documented code that was no longer here.
//
//  1. cancel() ALWAYS, and watch ALWAYS. Two failure modes look identical and
//     each is the other's cure. WEDGED: the engine sits at speaking === true
//     with nothing playing, and a speak() queues behind a ghost that never
//     ends; only cancel() clears that. SWALLOWED: a speak() issued straight
//     after a cancel() is sometimes dropped; only a retry clears that. Making
